      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>Rabbi Zalman Schachter-Shalomi, z”l, included “Another version of the [Weekday] Amidah” in his <tei:hi rend="italic">Siddur Tehillat Hashem Yidaber Pi</tei:hi> (2009). While I have set his text side-by-side with the wording of a sefaradi nusaḥ, it’s clear to me from Reb Zalman’s abbreviated text of most of the blessings, that he was inspired by the Weekday Amidah found in Seder Ḥibbur Berakhot, the earliest example of Italian liturgy. There, only a short introduction is offered before each corresponding blessing. –Aharon N. Varady</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_30340_notes"/>
